.TH "DEDB LS" "1" "2026-01-01" "0.0.18" "dedb ls Manual"
.SH NAME
dedb\-ls \- List downloaded games.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dedb ls
[OPTIONS] [PATTERNS]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
List downloaded games.
.PP
With no PATTERNS, lists every download. Each PATTERN is a shell
wildcard (*, ?, [...]), optionally <scheme>:-qualified, matched
against the downloaded names - e.g. `dedb ls 'gog:*jazz*'`.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-b,\fP \-\-backend SCHEME
Backend(s) to list, repeatable or comma-separated. Default: all (gog, archive).
.TP
\fB\-s,\fP \-\-short
Bare name; `<scheme>:` prefix only when >1 backend owns the name. (default)
.TP
\fB\-1\fP
Bare names only, deduplicated.
.TP
\fB\-l,\fP \-\-long
Every entry as a full `<scheme>:<id>` target (pasteable into `dedb run`).
.TP
\fB\-v,\fP \-\-verbose
Columns: target, title, classification, converted?, launch profiles.
.TP
\fB\-u,\fP \-\-url
The game's page on its origin site (archive.org item, GOG store page); falls back to `<scheme>:<id>` for a backend with no web page.
.TP
\fB\-\-href\fP
Wrap each entry in an ANSI (OSC 8) hyperlink to its origin-site page.
